nodes.body:
@xiaohaifeng1999 Thanks for the thorough cross-check, and for mapping all four heads on the combined sample!

I confirmed it locally. The newline corruption isn't specific to this PR: on `main`, any real newline inside a string already comes out joined with `", "` (e.g. `'line one\nline two.'` → `'line one, line two.'`). That's #60421. This PR only lets the combined sample reach that existing path instead of dropping the call.

So I'd rather not duplicate #60436's newline handling here. Once it lands, I'll rebase, run the candidate check through `_parse_newline_separated_calls` as discussed, and add your combined sample as a regression test so both fixes are covered together.

